  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Nigeria - Feasibility studies for the Nigeria Innovation Programme (NIP)</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="FR">Nigeria - &#xc9;tudes de faisabilit&#xe9; pour le programme d&apos;innovation du Nigeria (NIP)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Citizens of Nigeria in the Technology and Creative sectors and the innovation  ecosystem  to  understand  the  ecosystem dynamics,  challenges,  opportunities  and  relevant  models for catalysing growth through innovation in Nigeria. These include private and public sector participants such as investors, capacity development providers, enterprise support organisations, foundations,   venture   capital   firms   and   government ministries/agencies.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="FR"></narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The programme aims to boost innovation and job creation by further developing the technology and creativity entrepreneurship ecosystem i Nigeria. It comprises four complementing pillars including human capital, infrastructure, financing and enabling environment</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="FR"></narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To conduct a detailed feasibility study to assess the adequacy and operational effectiveness of key proposed interventions for the Nigeria Innovation Programme. The feasibility will lead to the detailed design of the programme including the detailed activities, economic viability of the programme, costing and impact, partnerships to be leveraged, and the Monitoring and Evaluation framework for implementation</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="FR"></narrative>
  </description>
